    "publishedAt": "2026-11-09",
    "summary": "ASRock Rack is promising up to 4 TB of DDR5 on a single socket with its DMRD16-2L+, one of the first motherboards built for Intel's upcoming Xeon 7 \"Diamond Rapids\" processors. Populate all 16 slots with those, and you hit 4 TB, along with a theoretical bandwidth of roughly 1.6 TB/s. Expansion is unusual, with no standard PCIe slots and no OCP NIC 3.0 connector. ASRock Rack fits it all on a 12 x 13-inch EEB PCB, about the size of a large E-ATX board, so it could squeeze into some bigger workstation cases.",
